CAT = "sgvlPassenger"; SEG = "PAS"
# Paper A: engaging with and handling passengers.
Q = [
("A passenger gets into your taxi. What should you do first?",
 "Greet them and confirm the destination", ["Start driving towards the city straight away", "Ask how they plan to pay", "Ask which app they usually use"],
 "A greeting and a quick check of the destination start the trip well and avoid wrong-address disputes later."),
("A passenger names a road you do not know. What is the best response?",
 "Say so and agree the route", ["Guess and correct the route later on", "Drive towards town and ask again there", "Ask them to take another taxi"],
 "Being honest and agreeing the route, using a map or app, avoids a dispute over the fare and the way taken."),
("A passenger disputes the fare at the end of a trip. How should you handle it?",
 "Stay calm and explain the charges", ["Lock the doors until they pay", "Raise your voice so they back down", "Keep their bag as security"],
 "Explain the meter or app fare and any surcharges politely. If it cannot be settled, record the details and let the operator or the authorities deal with it."),
("A passenger shouts at you because of heavy traffic. What should you do?",
 "Stay polite and keep driving safely", ["Shout back so that they calm down", "Stop and order them out of the car", "Turn the music up loudly"],
 "Staying calm and courteous usually defuses anger. Ending the hire without a reasonable excuse before the destination is an offence."),
("Which remark to a passenger could lead to demerit points?",
 "An insulting or harassing comment", ["A polite question about the route", "A request to fasten the seat belt", "A reminder about the fare shown"],
 "Verbally insulting, intimidating or harassing a passenger is an offence under the vocational licence rules and carries demerit points."),
("A passenger is talking on the phone and seems busy. How should you treat conversation?",
 "Keep it brief and let them lead", ["Ask personal questions to be friendly", "Talk about your own problems", "Comment on their phone call"],
 "Good service means reading the passenger. Some like to chat; many want quiet. Never ask intrusive personal questions."),
("You find a wallet on the back seat after a passenger leaves. What must you do?",
 "Hand it in as the rules require", ["Keep it until someone calls you about it", "Post a photo of it online to find the owner", "Give it to the next passenger"],
 "Property left in the vehicle must be deposited as the rules require. Holding it for more than 24 hours, and especially for seven days or more, brings demerit points."),
("A passenger calls about a phone they left in your car. What should you do?",
 "Help them get it back properly", ["Ask for a reward before saying anything", "Say you did not see a phone in the car", "Keep it if they were rude to you"],
 "Help the passenger recover their property, following your operator's lost property process and the rules on depositing it."),
("A passenger asks you to wait while they run into a shop. What should you make clear?",
 "How waiting time is charged", ["That waiting is never allowed", "That they must leave a deposit", "That you will leave after a minute"],
 "On a metered trip, waiting time is charged by the meter. Telling the passenger first avoids a dispute later."),
("A passenger is visibly drunk and unsteady. What is the best approach?",
 "Be patient and get them home safely", ["Refuse the hire at once without any reason", "Leave them at the roadside halfway there", "Lecture them about drinking"],
 "A drunk passenger still needs a safe trip. Stay calm and polite; if they become violent or abusive, stop safely and call the police."),
("A passenger tells you they feel threatened by someone following them. What should you do?",
 "Go to a safe place; offer to call 999", ["Tell them it is not your problem to solve", "Drop them at the nearest street corner", "Drive faster, even through red lights"],
 "Your role is to keep the passenger safe within the law. A busy, well-lit place and a call to 999 are the right steps."),
("A passenger asks you to switch off the air-conditioning. What should you do?",
 "Adjust it to their comfort", ["Refuse, as you set the cabin", "Ask them to pay extra for it", "Switch it off and open all windows"],
 "Within reason, the cabin temperature should suit the passenger. Small comforts shape how they rate the trip."),
("Your passenger leaves a negative comment about your driving. How should you respond?",
 "Reflect on it and improve", ["Find their home address", "Message them to argue", "Report them for no reason"],
 "Feedback helps you improve. Contacting a passenger to argue, or using their details for anything outside the trip, is unprofessional and may break the law."),
("A passenger asks for your personal number to book you directly next time. What should you consider?",
 "Bookings must follow your licence rules", ["Any private deal with a passenger is allowed", "Only cash jobs need to go through an app", "Taxis may not take repeat customers"],
 "A private hire car may only take passengers on a booking made through a licensed or licence-exempt operator. Street pick-ups and touting are offences."),
("Your passenger wants to bring an open durian into the car. What is a fair response?",
 "Explain politely and suggest sealing it", ["Shout at them and drive away", "Charge a cleaning fee on the spot in cash", "Throw the fruit out of the window"],
 "Explain calmly why a strong-smelling item is a problem, and look for a fair solution such as sealing it in a bag, rather than an argument."),
("A family has more passengers than your car has seat belts. What should you do?",
 "Take only as many as there are seats", ["Let a child sit on an adult's lap", "Put one passenger in the boot", "Take them all if the trip is short"],
 "Carrying more passengers than seats is unsafe and breaks the rules. Help them book a larger vehicle."),
("A passenger asks you to take a different route from the one your app shows. What should you do?",
 "Follow it if it is safe and legal", ["Insist on the route the app shows", "Stop the trip there and ask them out", "Take the longest route to teach them"],
 "The passenger may choose the route. Confirm it so there is no argument about the fare later."),
("Which personal habit most affects a passenger's comfort?",
 "A clean car", ["Loud music that you enjoy", "Eating your lunch while driving", "A strong air freshener"],
 "A tidy car and a neat, clean appearance show professionalism. Loud music, eating and strong scents bother many passengers."),
("A passenger is crying quietly in the back seat. What is the most respectful response?",
 "Give them privacy", ["Ask what happened to them in detail", "Post about it on social media later", "Tell them to stop crying"],
 "Respect the passenger's privacy. You can gently ask if they are all right, but do not pry."),
("A passenger asks you to stop the meter and accept a lump sum instead. What should you do?",
 "Decline and keep the meter on", ["Agree if they pay the whole amount in cash", "Agree for trips to the airport", "Agree if no one finds out"],
 "Street-hail taxi fares are charged by the meter. Demanding or taking a fare outside the pricing policy is an offence that carries demerit points."),
("A passenger starts filming you with their phone during an argument. How should you respond?",
 "Stay calm and polite", ["Grab the phone from them", "Film them back and post it", "Threaten to call their employer"],
 "Calm, professional behaviour protects you. A recording of you staying courteous is the best record of the event."),
("A passenger lights a cigarette in your car. What should you do?",
 "Ask them politely to stop", ["Ignore it to keep the peace", "Join them while waiting", "Stop on the expressway shoulder"],
 "Smoking is prohibited in taxis, and in private hire cars on paid chauffeured service since 1 October 2017. Ask politely; if they refuse, stop at a safe place and seek help."),
("Your passenger is a tourist who speaks little English. What helps most?",
 "Confirm it on a map", ["Speak louder and faster in English", "Guess which hotel they probably mean", "Refuse the hire"],
 "Showing the address on a phone map or the booking screen avoids taking a tourist to the wrong place."),
("At the end of a trip, what should you remind passengers to do?",
 "Check for their belongings", ["Rate you five stars in the app", "Pay a tip in cash", "Close all the windows before leaving"],
 "A quick reminder to check for phones, bags and wallets prevents most lost property."),
("A passenger asks you to drive while they sleep and wake them on arrival. What should you do?",
 "Drive smoothly and wake them gently", ["Take a longer route while they sleep", "Stop for your own errands", "Leave them asleep at the kerb"],
 "A sleeping passenger relies on your honesty. Take the agreed or most direct route and wake them politely at the destination."),
("A passenger tries to talk politics and you disagree strongly. What is professional?",
 "Stay neutral and politely move on", ["Argue the point until they agree", "End the trip early", "Ignore them completely"],
 "Keeping the conversation neutral and courteous avoids conflict. Your job is a safe, pleasant trip."),
("Why should you keep a record when a passenger becomes violent?",
 "To give facts to police and operator", ["To post the whole story online", "To refuse them on future trips only", "To claim a higher fare for the trip"],
 "Writing down the time, place and what happened helps the police and your operator deal with the incident."),
("A passenger asks you to help lift a heavy suitcase into the boot. What should you do?",
 "Help, lifting safely", ["Refuse, as luggage is the passenger's job", "Charge a separate fee for it", "Put it on the back seat unsecured"],
 "Helping with luggage is part of good service. Bend your knees and keep the load close to avoid injury."),
("A passenger asks you to stop at a petrol station toilet on a long trip. What is reasonable?",
 "Stop safely and wait for them", ["Refuse and keep driving to the address", "End the trip there", "Leave them and take another job"],
 "Reasonable requests should be met where safe. The trip continues once they return."),
("A passenger offers you a tip. What is correct?",
 "Thank them; never ask for one", ["Demand one on every trip you make", "Add it to the meter reading", "Hold back change until tipped"],
 "Tips are voluntary. Keeping change or pressing a passenger for money harms trust and may break the fare rules."),
("A passenger compliments you and asks for your name for the operator. What should you do?",
 "Point them to your ID", ["Give them a made-up name", "Refuse, as names are secret", "Give them your home address"],
 "Your identification is displayed so passengers can identify you. They can use it to give feedback through the operator."),
("Two passengers start fighting in the back seat. What should you do?",
 "Stop safely and call the police", ["Keep driving to the destination quickly", "Join in to separate them", "Speed up so they stop"],
 "A fight in the car is dangerous for everyone. Pull over where it is safe, get out if needed and call 999."),
]
